  "result": "Perfect! I found the document. The file `docs/adr/ADR-018-webhook-retry-policy.md` is an Architecture Decision Record that records exactly what you're asking about:\n\n- **Decision**: Webhook deliveries are queued (via `webhookRepo.enqueueDelivery()`) rather than sent inline within the same request\n- **Context/Reasoning**: The inline approach would cause latency coupling where slow or unreachable webhook endpoints would stall the triggering mutation (e.g., an issue status change request). The document explains this was identified as a problem before shipping.\n- **Alternatives considered**: The document has a dedicated \"Alternatives considered\" section covering:\n  1. Inline delivery (the original approach, now superseded)\n  2. Fixed-delay retry vs. exponential backoff\n  3. Unlimited retry attempts vs. a fixed ceiling\n\nThe decision was accepted in March 2026 and is related to several requirements (REQ-154 through REQ-161) and other ADRs (ADR-005, ADR-016, ADR-011).\n\nANSWER: docs/adr/ADR-018-webhook-retry-policy.md",
